 "stimulus_html": "Use negative exponents to rewrite the following expressions with no denominator:",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 506016,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{{{6^3}}}{{{{13}^8}}}\">\\frac{{{6^3}}}{{{{13}^8}}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"6^3 \\times {13^{ - 8}}\">6^3 \\times {13^{ - 8}}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Use the negative exponent rule. <span data-math=\"{a^{ - n}} = \\frac{1}{{{a^n}}}\"></span> provided that <i>a</i> ≠ 0.</p>\n<p>The negative exponent rule lets you say <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{{{{13}^8}}}\"></span> is equal to <span data-math=\"{13^{ - 8}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{6^3}}}{{{{13}^8}}} = {6^3} \\times {13^{ - 8}}\"></span></p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
